From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp, windows.ui.composition: Implement the transform and
 effect-factory objects consumed by the WinAppSDK title-bar bridge

Measured abort point.  With the Windows App Runtime 1.6 framework package
deployed (prefix data, README) the islands coordinator chain resolves and
the title-bar object reaches its content pass: the app dies at 11-12 s in
Window.set_ExtendsContentIntoTitleBar, 2/2 baseline runs, with a native
fault inside the coreclr interop transition (first-chance c0000005,
record addr coreclr.dll+0x18948f, faulting rip coreclr.dll+0x255429,
captured with -all,err+all,+module,+seh on 6x60 s batteries) that coreclr
AV-interop converts to System.AccessViolationException at the transition
frame and coreclr escalates via RaiseFailFastException.  One of the null
intermediates on that path is the transform set the composition backdrop
built during the ExtendsContentIntoTitleBar update: every device transform
creator of dlls/dcomp was an E_NOTIMPL FIXME stub, and the bridge does not
check the HRESULT of void-signature ABI calls, so a stub returning through
an untouched out-parameter feeds a null transform into the visual tree.
The Windows.UI.Composition effect factory used by the WinUI backdrop
brush pipeline was the same shape (E_NOTIMPL out of ICompositor
CreateEffectFactory / CreateEffectFactoryWithProperties on the
dlls/windows.ui.composition compositor).

Changes.  dlls/dcomp gains dlls/dcomp/transform.c: a real transform object
(dcomp_transform) answering IUnknown and the concrete
IDCompositionTranslateTransform, IDCompositionScaleTransform,
IDCompositionRotateTransform, IDCompositionSkewTransform,
IDCompositionMatrixTransform and IDCompositionMatrixTransform3D vtables
with property storage (offsets, scale, angle, axis, matrix3x2) and
owner-device tracking; device.c replaces the six E_NOTIMPL creators
(Translate, Scale, Rotate, Skew, Matrix, Matrix3D) with real
constructions, and dcomp_private.h declares the object.
dlls/windows.ui.composition replaces the E_NOTIMPL CreateEffectFactory /
CreateEffectFactoryWithProperties with a real
ICompositionEffectFactory / ICompositionEffectFactoryWithProperties
object and the effect brush object the factory produces (objects.c,
private.h), QI-complete for IUnknown, IAgileObject, ICompositionObject
and the composition effect interfaces.  No application-specific offsets,
no binary patching.

Measured on WhatsApp Desktop 2.2620.102.0, 6x60 s (-all,err+all,+module,
+seh, Xvfb :97, dev tree protocol 950): 2/6 alive 60 s clean (FailFast 0,
c0000005 0, exceptions 0), 4/6 die at 12 s with the same
set_ExtendsContentIntoTitleBar transition AV (fault rip coreclr.dll+
0x255429, deterministic across runs); baseline before this change 2/2
runs dead at 11-12 s with the same frame.  WebView2Loader.dll load count
and msedgewebview2.exe processes remain 0 in all runs, clean included.
